## Slide 6

Job Planned vs. Actual

Job Table Structures

Planned
Describes which System on which a Job will run.
Could be populated when Job is imported/created from ERP.
Could be populated as a result of TrakSYS APS.

Actual
Record of actual System (and times) on which a Job was run.
Populated automatically by the Logic Service when it detects start and end points for a Job.
 Can contain many child records for a single parent Job.

tJob
tJobSystemPlanned
tJobSystemActual
1 : N

## Slide 7

Material Planned vs. Actual

Job Table Structures

Planned
Sometimes known as the Bill of Materials (BOM)
Lists Materials and quantities to be consumed for a Job
Typically populated when Job is imported/created from ERP

Actual
Record of actual Material consumptions for a Job
Includes actual Quantities and source Batch/Lot Identifiers
Typically populated as consumptions are logged using user interfaces or scripts.

tJob
tMaterialUsePlanned
tMaterialUseActual